<details open><summary>What the specialist sales actually said · before versus after the move</summary><p>Four houses appear in the reviewed pre-weekend META timeline. Repeating the same App Store event is corroboration across distributors, not four independent catalysts. Client usage, desk opinion, PB observations and research relays retain different labels.</p><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-16 · 11:43 UTC · UBS</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Positioning opinion / client conversations · Positive, with event risk</b></p><p>Reports little long-only sponsorship pending credible ROI evidence; investors ask whether Connect expectations are too high. Desk expects short-term weakness to attract buyers.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>Dwyer, Christina · UBS TMI: 09/16/2026: A return of the UBS Ad Checks, META Connect, Zuck&#x27;s manifesto pt 2, FOMC, East Coast Payments &amp; FinTech Discussion (NYC), Key Events, Headlines, Access &amp; More</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC0005864836270000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-16 · 13:07 UTC · Bernstein</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Positioning opinion / client conversations · Positive, with sidelined investors</b></p><p>Reports improving META sentiment, some investors on the sidelines because of a potential equity raise, and greater willingness to own META than GOOGL. No measured holdings or confirmed equity offering.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>SEIDMAN Tyler · Bernstein Tech: Clarity fails but N/T visibility to improve, Texas data center progress (= +), UBER expands with Costco (+ -), TKO setup (= +), Quick thought on META/GOOGL sentiment / positioning</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC0005864836740000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-18 · 12:10 UTC · JPMorgan</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Adoption milestone relayed by sales · Adoption confirmation</b></p><p>Highlights Muse at number one in the App Store and asks which usage KPIs Connect might disclose. The ranking is a shared underlying event, not a separate discovery by each broker.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>Mark Schilsky - Specialist Sales - US TMT · JPM TECH SKETCH: META Muse is #1, EBAY/RDDT Alt Data Updates, Whatnot Lowers Commissions (re: EBAY), AT&amp;T Convergence Momentum, INTU Investor Day Meh</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058792CAD00000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-18 · 12:10 UTC · UBS</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Desk flow / PB book commentary · Mixed / pair unwinding</b></p><p>Says the long META / short GOOGL pair continues to unwind into Connect and investors expect sell-the-news risk. Calls GOOGL the most crowded Mag 7 long in the UBS PB book, potentially reflecting short covering. This is not evidence that META is the most crowded long.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>Dwyer, Christina · UBS TMI: 09/18/2026: 14 Highest Conviction TMT Ideas, TMT Happy Hour TODAY, T Preview, Long META vs Short GOOGL, NFLX, AAPL, PB Update (Comm services lowest net exposure), SPCX rebal, Telco (AI losers??), Key Events, Headlines, Access &amp; More</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058792CAD10000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-18 · 13:41 UTC · Morgan Stanley</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Research thesis relayed by sales · Positive / monetization thesis</b></p><p>Connects Muse adoption with Brian Nowak&#x27;s agentic playbook and conditional 2028 EPS sensitivities. A research scenario, not realized revenue or a client position.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>Tom Wigg · MS TMT 9.18:  META Muse No. 1 + MS Agentic Playbook bullish META SHOP AMZN vs mixed Gig Econ + OTAs; GOOGL Gemini 4 + Agent debate; MS Credit Hyperscale CDS basket; Databricks; Tokens + Crypto; COHR / ECOC preview; ASML SNDK COHR CIFR HUBS INTU ORANGE</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058792CB170000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-18 · 15:39 UTC · Bernstein</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Client conversations / price reaction · Positive product, event caution</b></p><p>Notes App Store leadership while the stock is down; describes positive client conversations but profit taking after the prior rally and risk of buying the news before selling the event.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>SEIDMAN Tyler · Bernstein Tech: Mid-day moves: NFLX feedback, META overtakes ChatGPT in app store, Cyber downgrade feedback, EBAY strength, Digital assets thoughts, CN Internet into Trump-Xi next week, DKNG weakness</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058792CB4F0000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-18 · 16:47 UTC · Morgan Stanley</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Client and colleague product-use anecdotes · Positive, with some failures</b></p><p>Muse Cases collects actual reported uses: tickets, bill negotiation, purchases, hotel comparison and reservations; some tasks failed. These are anecdotes about product utility, not independently measured adoption or security purchases.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>Tom Wigg · MS TMT:  Muse Cases  🦞  META Muse ushers in the consumer Agent era or &#x27;OpenClaw for normies&#x27;.  I polled coworkers + clients for the best use cases thus far.  $MSXXCLAW Agentic basket.  Brian Nowak Agent Playbook.</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058792CB600000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-21 · 11:41 UTC · UBS</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Pre-open expectations / client conversations · Bullish medium term, event caution</b></p><p>Before Monday&#x27;s open, describes bullish META sentiment, limited long-only sponsorship and an increasingly sell-the-news setup for Connect. A view about positioning, not a position census.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>Dwyer, Christina · UBS TMI: 09/21/2026: META Connect, Consumer Concerns, PB Update (Hyperscaler vs Semis), Ad Checks, Fiber Call,  Key Events, Headlines, Access &amp; More</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC0005890D1A580000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-21 · 12:15 UTC · Bernstein</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Client inquiries / product friction · Mixed / competitive risk</b></p><p>Reports growing inquiries about horizontal-agent risk to AMZN and news that Amazon blocked Muse; clients are generally not very worried about AMZN given Alexa+ and logistics. Increased discussion can concern a risk to another stock.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>SEIDMAN Tyler · Bernstein Tech: Semi’s bus tour takeaways, AMZN isn’t aMUSEd (+ -), Tokenization deep-dive post Clarity Act, The PSKY settlement trade (= +), Thoughts on DIS (+ -), Cyber + tokenization opportunity for V/MA</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC0005890D1A750000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-21 · 12:50 UTC · Morgan Stanley</b> <span class="narr-tag">Before Monday open</span></div><p><b>Pre-open product news · Adoption confirmation / access friction</b></p><p>Reports Muse retained App Store leadership over the weekend and Amazon blocked agent access. Received after the 08:30 ET tweet cut and before the 09:30 ET open.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>Tom Wigg · MS TMT 9.21:  META Muse No 1 vs AMZN blocks; GOOGL Gemini hack + CC asst; PANW CRWD / AI Safety + Cyber 1.5% AI spend vs 4% Bull Case; NVDA / Power Shortfall 57GW &#x27;28; MRVL bullish preview; DELL HPE P update; AAPL TSLA SPCX ORCL APP U PSKY DIS PAGS ZETA</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC0005890D1A910000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article><article class="narr-note"><div><b>2026-09-21 · 17:25 UTC · UBS</b> <span class="narr-tag">AFTER THE RALLY</span></div><p><b>Post-move desk flow report and interpretation · Crowded by holders, limited size / little LO flow</b></p><p>After the stock was already up about 10%, says UBS is not seeing long-only funds drive the flow. Desk characterizes META as a crowded HF long without large sizing and interprets the move as fast-money positioning, possibly retail. This is post-move diagnosis, excluded from any pre-open signal.</p><details><summary>Original email reference</summary><p>Dwyer, Christina · UBS TMI: Midday Round Up (9/21) - Muse Mania</p><p><a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC0005890D1B170000">Open original in Outlook</a> · exact received time retained in local evidence.</p></details></article></details>
<details open><summary>Parallel episodes, including failures</summary><p>Pre-open discussion only: a 24-hour window ending 08:30 ET, except the 64.5-hour Monday weekend window. Counts across different window lengths are not directly comparable. Examples were selected retrospectively by narrative mechanism, not by a systematic alert.</p><div style="overflow:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>Episode</th><th>Hours</th><th>Posts</th><th>Other authors</th><th>Gap</th><th>Open → last</th><th>Day</th><th>vs QQQ</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>META<br><small>2026-09-09</small></td><td>24.0</td><td>28</td><td>7</td><td>5.73%</td><td>0.78%</td><td>6.55%</td><td>6.84 pp</td></tr><tr><td>META<br><small>2026-09-18</small></td><td>24.0</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>0.92%</td><td>-3.32%</td><td>-2.43%</td><td>-3.06 pp</td></tr><tr><td>META<br><small>2026-09-21</small></td><td>64.5</td><td>55</td><td>12</td><td>2.18%</td><td>8.96%</td><td>11.34%</td><td>8.56 pp</td></tr><tr><td>NBIS<br><small>2026-09-17</small></td><td>24.0</td><td>7</td><td>4</td><td>9.86%</td><td>-5.23%</td><td>4.12%</td><td>2.39 pp</td></tr><tr><td>ORCL<br><small>2026-09-11</small></td><td>24.0</td><td>13</td><td>2</td><td>7.51%</td><td>-8.61%</td><td>-1.74%</td><td>-2.61 pp</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li><b>META 2026-09-09:</b> First full session after the Sep 8 product launch; announcement is a confound.</li><li><b>META 2026-09-18:</b> App Store milestone already circulating; a negative-price counterexample despite positive product discussion.</li><li><b>META 2026-09-21:</b> Weekend diffusion plus Monday analyst price-target hike; selected after observing the rally.</li><li><b>NBIS 2026-09-17:</b> GPU pricing narrative: potentially measurable monetization; investigate contract terms and capacity.</li><li><b>ORCL 2026-09-11:</b> Cloud demand / backlog narrative around earnings; financing and capex offset enthusiasm.</li></ul><p><b>NBIS illustrates the entry problem:</b> positive close-to-close performance coexisted with a negative open-to-close return. ORCL illustrates an attention spike followed by reversal. These cases do not establish forecasting power.</p></details>
<details><summary>Reviewed weekend tone and source links · 18 non-company posts</summary><p>Assistant context review of the actual posts; no independently labelled model evaluation. Repeated posts from one author do not create extra independent opinions. Positive infrastructure read-through is not assigned to META stock sentiment.</p><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/bubbleboi/status/2101068973899153743">@bubbleboi · 2026-09-18 22:00 UTC</a><p><b>positive adoption thesis</b> · Consumer-agent diffusion is part of a broad market thesis; no META trade disclosed.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/SouthernValue95/status/2101139898103103755">@SouthernValue95 · 2026-09-19 02:42 UTC</a><p><b>positive direct-use anecdote</b> · Author reports building a game with Muse.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/jukan05/status/2101163050367955130">@jukan05 · 2026-09-19 04:14 UTC</a><p><b>availability question</b> · Question about Korean availability; no directional view inferred.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/SouthernValue95/status/2101176940342231195">@SouthernValue95 · 2026-09-19 05:09 UTC</a><p><b>positive direct-use anecdote</b> · Author praises Muse despite having no technical ability; same author as prior demo.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/jukan05/status/2101285687719030873">@jukan05 · 2026-09-19 12:22 UTC</a><p><b>positive product thesis / unverified report</b> · Praises progress from OpenClaw; VM-rental claim is hearsay.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/patrickc/status/2101296407433076738">@patrickc · 2026-09-19 13:04 UTC</a><p><b>commercial partner announcement</b> · Stripe cofounder promoting a commercial integration; separated from other voices.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/QQ_Timmy/status/2101305031911989707">@QQ_Timmy · 2026-09-19 13:38 UTC</a><p><b>mixed / third-party recap</b> · Recaps a podcast on adoption, safety and control; not an independent META recommendation.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/Midnight_Captl/status/2101358516489646340">@Midnight_Captl · 2026-09-19 17:11 UTC</a><p><b>positive infrastructure read-through</b> · CPU demand/revision hypothesis; not a bullish META holding signal.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/SouthernValue95/status/2101481719241077078">@SouthernValue95 · 2026-09-20 01:21 UTC</a><p><b>positive direct-use anecdote</b> · Three games described; same author, one author vote rather than three.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/FredaDuan/status/2101514280835403852">@FredaDuan · 2026-09-20 03:30 UTC</a><p><b>positive consumer-agent thesis</b> · Discusses separation of work and personal agents and several potential winners; no stock action.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/wallstengine/status/2101656117424402644">@wallstengine · 2026-09-20 12:53 UTC</a><p><b>advertisement relayed</b> · Shares a Muse commercial; not evidence of paid adoption.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/deedydas/status/2101704962426478918">@deedydas · 2026-09-20 16:08 UTC</a><p><b>positive direct-use anecdote</b> · Lists completed tasks and useful workflows across Muse and Instinct; not exclusive Muse attribution.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/borrowed_ideas/status/2101805512404910293">@borrowed_ideas · 2026-09-20 22:47 UTC</a><p><b>positive direct-use anecdote</b> · Reports building a game with Muse without mentioning META; alias mapping captures it.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/DanielTNiles/status/2101832568706679031">@DanielTNiles · 2026-09-21 00:35 UTC</a><p><b>positive META attributes / cautious macro</b> · META is among companies with distribution and cash-flow advantages; overall market view is cautious.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/zephyr_z9/status/2101901218390188226">@zephyr_z9 · 2026-09-21 05:07 UTC</a><p><b>positive infrastructure read-through</b> · Agent adoption linked to NAND demand; no META stock stance inferred.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/FundaAI/status/2101905790739296536">@FundaAI · 2026-09-21 05:26 UTC</a><p><b>research agenda / no directional Muse label</b> · Weekly research digest advertises a Muse monetization interview; no directional label assigned.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/barronsonline/status/2101998921924870364">@barronsonline · 2026-09-21 11:36 UTC</a><p><b>post-move news about other stocks</b> · Headline on Intel and Arm jumping; not an independent Muse product review.</p></article><article class="narr-note"><a href="https://x.com/firstadopter/status/2101999272862331064">@firstadopter · 2026-09-21 11:37 UTC</a><p><b>adoption fact relayed</b> · Repeats number-one App Store ranking; no firsthand usage or stock purchase inferred.</p></article></details>
<details open><summary>How to look for the next case</summary><ol><li><b>Detect topic diffusion:</b> ticker + product + catalyst aliases; 6h / 24h / 72h windows; feed-normalised mentions; unique and newly participating authors; company/partner/news concentration.</li><li><b>Read the change in conviction:</b> compare each source with its own earlier view. Keep firsthand usage, monetization evidence, investment opinion, client inquiries and actual reported flows separate. Deduplicate the event across brokers.</li><li><b>Map participation and position size:</b> breadth of HF ownership, position sizing, LO sponsorship and PB net exposure are distinct. Missing holdings stay unknown; enthusiasm alone does not create a crowded-position label.</li><li><b>Test a frozen signal before the open:</b> log the cutoff and available source snapshot; compare next-open returns at +1/+3/+5/+20 sessions and later attention/desk diffusion. Control for prior return, broad/sector move, earnings and research changes. Include failed alerts and matched no-alert stocks.</li></ol><p>This overlay implements topic mappings, source-separated counts, a reviewed META desk/tone timeline and descriptive price parallels. Intraday collection, generic semantic desk labelling, event-wide deduplication and prospective alerts still require implementation and evaluation. There is no new fitted composite or automatic trade recommendation.</p></details>
<details><summary>Coverage, timestamps and competing catalysts</summary><ul><li>User-collected account sample, not the whole of X. Other accounts are not certified independent; affiliation list is incomplete. No follower/like weights or engagement captured after the move.</li><li>fetched_at is overwritten when engagement is refreshed, not immutable first_seen. A fetch before cutoff proves availability by then; a later fetch does not prove absence before cutoff. No full historical point-in-time backtest.</li><li>6,733 message metadata records scanned since Sep 7 in the primary Outlook store; 314 candidate bodies selected by specialist sender/subject. Online archive and attachments not exhaustively read; 11 META notes context-reviewed.</li><li>Case-selected retrospective description, not a validated leading factor. QQQ is a broad growth benchmark, not a sector-neutral hedge.</li><li>Bloomberg Desktop API / PX_LAST and PX_OPEN; downloaded 21 Sep 2026 after US regular close; same-day vendor marks, not audited final close</li></ul><p><a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/">Meta launched Muse on September 8</a>, before the observed weekend. <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/wells-fargo-adjusts-price-target-091922649.html">Wells Fargo raised its target to $796 from $640 before Monday's open</a>. Connect on September 23 was another expectation catalyst. The weekend is a diffusion case, not a causal attribution of Monday's return.</p><p>All 55 weekend posts have a stored fetch timestamp before the Monday 08:30 ET cut. This supports pre-open availability in the existing collection, not a claim that this overlay issued an alert at that time. The original weekly tracker remains dated separately below.</p></details>
</section></main></div></div><script>
(()=>{
 const button=document.querySelector('.rd-theme');
 if(button)button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
  const dark=document.documentElement.dataset.theme!=='dark';
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme=dark?'dark':'light';
  button.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(dark));
  button.setAttribute('aria-label',dark?'Switch to light theme':'Switch to dark theme');
 });
})();
</script></body></html>